{"blocks":[{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00496_f696f7abb4e1","block_type":"heading","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"context_only","text":"# XIII. Authoring Checklist\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00498_1754829b09e1","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"Before accepting authored prose, check:\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00500_3d479392624b","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"1. Are Defined Terms capitalized consistently?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00501_489ffcae86ec","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"2. Are ordinary nouns left lowercase?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00502_361c5fc6bd9f","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"3. Are only canonical experiential operators in ALL CAPS?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00503_ce67b2c680b7","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"4. Is the Register noun kept distinct from its operator?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00504_de8324087b98","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"5. Are MSIDs dot-delimited UpperCamelCase and shown in code style?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00505_e251d9064522","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"6. Does the Bare Core-Species Singular take singular agreement?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00506_eaf04d976fd6","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"7. Is a plural species noun used when the sentence concerns multiple animals or population behavior?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00507_cf0eaeae1112","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"8. Does every Hyphen-bound form follow its canonical internal casing?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00508_d53aabe90295","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"9. Is `Prior-life Tale` written with lowercase **life**?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00509_21851bffb22e","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"10. Is typography carrying one defined function rather than casual emphasis?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00510_93136a524844","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"11. Are provisional conventions marked as provisional in internal documents?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00511_bebe62330a1f","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"12. Can the sentence be understood without capitalization doing all the explanatory work?\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00515_6b7a9c613745","block_type":"heading","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"context_only","text":"# XIV. Machine-checkable Lint Rules\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00517_335adc8590dd","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"The authoring toolchain should eventually flag:\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00519_2f8f0c93cf4d","block_type":"code_fence","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"```text\nArchitecture.Register.Risk\nAway.RISK.Crossing\nArchitecture.Register.Travel\nAway.Travel\nPrior-Life Tale\nAfter-Name\nWood Mouse\nWood Mice\n```\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00521_b43119052059","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"It should also flag probable agreement errors:\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00523_77ad8e98bf61","block_type":"code_fence","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"```text\nMouse build\nRabbit gather\nSquirrel connect\n```\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00525_24e8462ef1a0","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"when `Mouse`, `Rabbit`, or `Squirrel` is being used as the Bare Core-Species Singular.\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00527_de4a1b2cf5e4","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"Linting should warn rather than automatically rewrite where context could indicate:\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00529_27c9cc20f4da","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"- a direct quotation;\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00530_87a0e9d7a2d5","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"- a historical source;\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00531_0e03656e2a65","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"- lowercase zoological usage;\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00532_89a98a0b389c","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"- a particular named Citizen;\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00533_bf93bd9ef691","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"- a heading or visual treatment;\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00534_d8e62625d6df","block_type":"list_item","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"- or an intentional plural construction.\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00538_5e630287c4cb","block_type":"heading","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"context_only","text":"# XV. Phonebook Appendix Plate\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00540_76136f7cc635","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"The Phonebook receives a one-page condensation provisionally titled:\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00542_3f1338d605c3","block_type":"heading","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"context_only","text":"## HOW MEDIAN WRITES\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00544_7790edc7c1c4","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Meaning | Written form | Example |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00545_5cb0682bc5ee","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"|---|---|---|\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00546_d0ac86eddae6","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Defined game noun | Initial Caps | Citizen, Place, Body Unit |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00547_d8b4d4382345","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Experiential operator | ALL CAPS | DWELL, TRAVEL, RISK |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00548_43afd5a39dca","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Semantic address | Dot-delimited UpperCamelCase | `Away.Crossing.Mouse` |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00549_2e7767238bfe","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Animal-language word | Hyphen-bound | After-name, Prior-life Tale |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00550_e06f9ac0451b","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Archetypal Core Species | Bare singular + singular agreement | Mouse builds a Manor House. |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00551_ecfcaf468d3a","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Stable text function | Defined typography | *mechanics-teaching Narrative* |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00553_4a0fffc79583","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"Footer doctrine:\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00555_26a691a594a8","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"> **Typography is part of MEDIAN's semantic system. It tells the reader whether a word is a game concept, an act of play, an ontological address, a translated animal word, or a particular kind of authored voice.**\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00557_ac73b3be46eb","block_type":"paragraph","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"The plate is generated from this guide and must not introduce independent conventions.\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00561_cac4c21268ee","block_type":"heading","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"context_only","text":"# XVI. Current Convention Ledger\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00563_3a6b18cfc9f0","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Convention | Status | Owner |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00564_5cb0682bc5ee","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"|---|---|---|\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00565_10d1329e2600","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Initial Caps for Defined Terms | `SETTLED` | Authorial Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00566_cf4e9e7e7385","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| ALL CAPS for experiential operators | `SETTLED` | Authorial Grammar, constrained by P&A |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00567_dec29eac1b02","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Dot-delimited UpperCamelCase MSIDs | `SETTLED` | MSID Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00568_06b7f7a404ad","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Bare Core-Species Singular | `SETTLED` | Authorial Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00569_5e65c0ffeabf","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Singular agreement for bare Core-Species names | `SETTLED` | Authorial Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00570_b7fe1714ba18","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Hyphen-bound animal-language compounds | `SETTLED` | Authorial Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00571_a6baa6292947","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| `Prior-life Tale` exact casing | `SETTLED` | Authorial Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00572_9eade0cb487e","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| Italics for mechanics-teaching Narrative | `PROVISIONAL` | Authorial Grammar |\n"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001__B00573_3a6dcb7e543e","block_type":"table_row","status_markers":[],"structural_disposition":"eligible","text":"| One-page Phonebook grammar plate | `SETTLED` as publication architecture | Authorial Grammar / Phonebook |\n"}],"ordinal_range":[496,576],"pilot_id":"M050-AUTHGRAM-PILOT-003","schema_version":"M050-PILOT-PAYLOAD-0.1","source_id":"M050-SRC-AUTHORIAL-GRAMMAR-001","source_sha256":"7d23ef2ccbff0c6594975c03cf405d838a3cc3f712ea6faf942581a72c9284ff"}
